<!--
  Entries to merge into the `flutter create .`-generated Info.plist.

  Unlike the camera or microphone, RPScreenRecorder doesn't need an
  NSUsageDescription key for the video itself - iOS shows its own
  system "Start Broadcast/Recording?" prompt regardless. This app does
  capture microphone audio alongside the screen (RPScreenRecorder's
  default), which does need one, and needs UIBackgroundModes so audio
  capture (and, by extension, socket I/O for the video/control
  channels) doesn't get suspended immediately if the app is briefly
  backgrounded mid-session.

  What this does NOT cover: true system-wide, background screen
  mirroring. `RPScreenRecorder.shared().startCapture(...)` (used by
  `ScreenCaptureBridge.swift`) only captures this app's own window
  while it's in the foreground - Apple's mechanism for capturing the
  whole screen from the background is a separate Broadcast Upload
  Extension target, which needs its own App Group entitlement and
  can't be added by editing a plist; see the README's "Deliberately
  deferred" section.
-->
<plist>
<dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Lets a remote viewer hear this phone's audio while its screen is being shared, if you choose to include it.</string>
    <key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
    <array>
        <string>audio</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
